Z||000000||firstfiero||04-12-2001||02:29 PM||||    I don't know if you guys saw but I found a junkyard with about 40 fieros in it. Anyway their are alot of perfect sil panels on the 84s, My question is will they fit my 86se and what is the best way of getting them off?   Thanks Todd <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||04-12-2001||02:45 PM||||Believe they should fit.<P>Here's a thread that should help: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005929.html" TARGET=_blank>84 Fiero Sail Panels</A><P>(That's my old screename BTW)<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||04-12-2001||03:17 PM||||If I remember correctly, the 85-88's used plastic and the 84's were glass (that's why they last). I haven't been able to get them to fit. If I'm missing a trick, I'd appreciate a note.<P>------------------<BR>85 SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||04-12-2001||03:22 PM||||They will fit, they do mount slighly differant but they will fit fine. And the 84's are glass, where the post 84s are plastic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||04-12-2001||03:42 PM||||I believe you need to take the entire assembly, glass and the frame, to mount in the later year cars.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||04-12-2001||05:15 PM||||So how do you go about removing these panels??  Cause I know of a junkyard that had a couple.  If I can get them for cheap I would pick them up. Most were from 85-88.  There were some 84 and all looked to be in good shape.<P>                                Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000006||Tina||04-12-2001||10:50 PM||||Remove upper seat belt bolt---<BR>Remove inside panel----------<BR>Now you should be able get to the nut <BR>holding it from the inside-<BR>(Aim for the area right behind the "arrow head")<BR>After that it's a piece of cake   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||04-13-2001||04:01 PM||||The glass are a bit shorter in the diagonal from the plastic so if the plastic panels rubbed some of the panel off, the glass panels won't cover it. On one Fiero, I used touch up paint, but on the other I added a black friction strip to cover the area.<P>Minor detail.<P>Also, you must have the spring steel clips to install the glass panels.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jake2m4||04-15-2001||01:23 PM||||I'm currently working on putting the glass '84 panels onto the plastic backing/frame of my '85.  I pretty much tore them off of an 84 in the junk yard and just kept the glass part.  I'm going to take the plastic part off of the ones on my car and put the glass in its place.  It looks like it will fit great.<P>------------------<BR>'85 Fiero Sport Coupe<BR>'95 Pontiac Grand AM SE||||reg||1
